Chapter: Ecdsa Sha384
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter EcdsaP256

 The P-256 pair is the case that mattered: the elliptic-curve
 intermediates of Sectigo and Let's Encrypt are P-256 keys signed under
 SHA-384, and X509Chain answered False for that combination until the
 digest half was written.

 Both vectors are OpenSSL's. It generated each key, signed "sample" under
 SHA-384, and verified its own signature before these bytes were taken,
 so ours is the second implementation to see them.

