Section: Cases

  p256-ok : Boolean = ecdsa-p256-verify-sha384 k256-pub s-msg k256-sig

  p384-ok : Boolean = ecdsa-p384-verify-sha384 k384-pub s-msg k384-sig

 THE DIGEST IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE, so it is asserted directly: the
 same key, message and signature under the SHA-256 entry point must FAIL.
 Without these two lines the file would pass unchanged if both entry
 points hashed with SHA-256, which is the substitution X509Chain's prose
 warns about.

  p256-wrong-digest : Boolean = ecdsa-p256-verify k256-pub s-msg k256-sig

  p384-wrong-digest : Boolean = ecdsa-p384-verify k384-pub s-msg k384-sig

  p256-bad-r : Boolean =
    ecdsa-p256-verify-sha384 k256-pub s-msg (list-set-at k256-sig 0 (bit-xor (list-at k256-sig 0) 1))

  p256-bad-s : Boolean =
    ecdsa-p256-verify-sha384 k256-pub s-msg (list-set-at k256-sig 60 (bit-xor (list-at k256-sig 60) 1))

  p256-bad-key : Boolean =
    ecdsa-p256-verify-sha384 (list-set-at k256-pub 20 (bit-xor (list-at k256-pub 20) 1)) s-msg k256-sig

  p256-bad-msg : Boolean = ecdsa-p256-verify-sha384 k256-pub s-alt k256-sig

  p384-bad-r : Boolean =
    ecdsa-p384-verify-sha384 k384-pub s-msg (list-set-at k384-sig 0 (bit-xor (list-at k384-sig 0) 1))

  p384-bad-msg : Boolean = ecdsa-p384-verify-sha384 k384-pub s-alt k384-sig

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("p256-sha384=" & show p256-ok)
    print-line-uni ("p384-sha384=" & show p384-ok)
    print-line-uni ("p256-under-sha256=" & show p256-wrong-digest)
    print-line-uni ("p384-under-sha256=" & show p384-wrong-digest)
    print-line-uni ("p256-bad-r=" & show p256-bad-r)
    print-line-uni ("p256-bad-s=" & show p256-bad-s)
    print-line-uni ("p256-bad-key=" & show p256-bad-key)
    print-line-uni ("p256-bad-msg=" & show p256-bad-msg)
    print-line-uni ("p384-bad-r=" & show p384-bad-r)
    print-line-uni ("p384-bad-msg=" & show p384-bad-msg)
